rConfig`. This is the modern way to register code-only parsers that work with `parse()`."},"796":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-75","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#the-inline-parser-signature","content":"An inline parser is an async function that takes a Buffer and returns an Artifact:"},"797":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-76","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#option-3-legacy-providers-deprecated","content":"The old `providers` registry is deprecated. Use `InlineParserDef` in `parserConfig` instead."},"798":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-77","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#option-3-legacy-providers-deprecated","content":"If you need backward compatibility, you can still use `fileToArtifact` with the providers registry:"},"799":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-78","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#option-3-legacy-providers-deprecated","content":"**Note:** This approach does not support MIME detection or the parser system — it only applies when you call `fileToArtifact` directly with an explicit `mimeType`."},"800":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-79","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#npm-package-parser","content":"Install a package that implements the `NpmParserModule` interface:"},"801":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-80","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#npm-package-parser","content":"When both `parseFile` and `parseStream` are exported, Struktur prefers `parseFile` for file inputs (zero-copy) and `parseStream` for buffer or stdin inpu